{title: 394 - Far From All Care}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #394 • PEVENSEY • 11.10.12.9}
{lyricist: D. A. R. Aufranc}
{composer: D. A. R. Aufranc}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 394}
{meta: tune PEVENSEY}
{meta: meter 11.10.12.9}
{meta: category Doctrines - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Far [Bb]from [C7/G]all [F]care we [Bb]hail the [F/C]Sabbath [C7]morning;
[F]O'er [Am]waving [Dm]fields and [Gm]from the distant [C]sea
[F]Swell notes [Dm]of praise [Gm]in harmony [C]resounding
[Bb]As all creation turns her [F/C]heart [C7]to [F]Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Though [Bb]man [C7/G]alone, [F]Lord, [Bb]of Thy [F/C]great [C]creation
[F]Fails now [Am]to laud [Dm]Thee for [Gm]Thy love and power,
[F]Yet still a [Dm]remnant [Gm/Bb]love Thee and [C]remember
[Bb]Thy holy law and each [F/C]sweet Sabbath hour.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]Lord [Bb]of [C7/G]the [F]Sabbath, [Bb]Savior [F/C]and [C]Creator,
[F]Calm [Am]now the [Dm]throbbings [Gm]of each troubled breast.
[F]Speak to our [Dm]hearts [Gm]the peace of Thy [C]commandments,
[Bb]Breathe on each soul fair Eden's [F/C]hallowed ret.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]Strong [Bb]in [C7/G]Thy [F]might and [Bb]quiet in [F/C]Thy [C]meekness,
[F]May [Am]we Thine [Dm]image [Gm]bear from day to [C]day.
[F]Then may we [Dm]enter [Gm]pearly gates [C]eternal
[Bb]And sing redemption's song [F/C]each Sabbath day.
{end_of_verse}
